    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0147" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Generalissimo
                        Chiang</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d78-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde
                                Park</hi></placeName>?] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-30"
                            >30 October 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President to Generalissimo
                    Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
                <p>I have not heard definitely from Marshal Stalin but there is still a chance of Churchill and me meeting him near Persian Gulf.</p>
                <pb facs="0148" n="56" xml:id="pg56"/>
                <p>Very confidentially, I hope you will make arrangements to meet with Churchill and me in general neighborhood of
                    Cairo about November twenty-sixth.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Best regards</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the American Military Mission to China, Chungking, via the White House
                    Map Room and Army channels, as telegram 3734, from the War Department to the
                    Mission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
